# Author name order was taken from this repository's commit metadata. CFF needs each name
# split into given and family parts, and that split is a guess for names where the
# convention is not written down — each author should correct their own entry.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CALIBER: operator-shift-robust conformal hallucination flagging for
  generative-prior image reconstruction
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Angshuman
    family-names: Chakravertty
  - given-names: Sai Krishna Reddy
    family-names: Kuchuru
  - given-names: Rayyan
    family-names: Md
repository-code: "https://github.com/Angshuman1211/CALIBER"
abstract: >-
  Conformal reliability certificates for image reconstruction assume the
  acquisition operator is fixed between calibration and deployment. This
  repository measures what happens when it is not. On sparse-view and
  limited-angle CT with a chest-CT diffusion prior, a transferred conformal
  threshold falls below its nominal 0.90 coverage at 36 of 72 ordered operator
  pairs, and in the worst pair catches 26.9 percent of hallucinated regions
  where it promises 90 percent. Group-conditional calibration restores nominal
  coverage at all nine operators. Four refinements that condition on how far
  the operator moved, rather than on which operator it is, were specified in
  advance and are each unsupported. A separate result concerns evaluation
  practice: where the generative prior does not match the anatomy, the field's
  standard protocol for validating an uncertainty map is outscored by a
  detector that reads no posterior information at all.
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - distribution-free uncertainty quantification
  - inverse problems
  - image reconstruction
  - hallucination detection
  - diffusion models
  - magnetic resonance imaging
  - computed tomography
  - distribution shift
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-26"
